{
  "rules": [
    "Strong persistent underprediction in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show an upswing, add an upward level shift to the whole path (model is ~5–15 EUR too low, increasing with horizon).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: error grows with lead time; apply a ramping uplift (small in days 1–3, larger by days 10–30).",
    "Trend/acceleration miss: after a breakout (new 30-day high), the model assumes mean reversion too early; instead extend the uptrend for ~2–3 weeks (higher slope) before flattening.",
    "Lag in capturing step-changes: when spot jumps >~2 EUR/day or >~4 EUR over 3 days, shift the forecast curve upward immediately rather than gradually (reduce delay).",
    "Over-smoothing volatility: peaks/troughs are muted; increase amplitude during strong momentum periods (e.g., scale deviations from the forecast mean by ~1.2–1.5 when recent realized vol is elevated)."
  ]
}
